⚡🇺🇸🇻🇪 A Venezuelan man, arrested near the White House with three firearms and related ammunition, told police that voices in his head ordered him to kill U.S. President Donald Trump, according to the Department of Homeland Security on Friday.

On Thursday evening, several agents from the U.S. Secret Service approached Ronny Yordrix Guanipa Chrinos after noticing his suspicious behavior inside a vehicle parked on Constitution Avenue in Washington, DC. During the encounter, Chrinos reportedly told the agents that voices in his head had ordered him to go to the capital and kill Trump.

